Assignment: Build a Machine Learning Classification Front-End
Objective

Design and develop a user-friendly front-end application that allows users to upload any CSV dataset, automatically preprocess the data, download the preprocessed dataset, select a machine learning classification algorithm, train the model, and evaluate its performance.

Functional Requirements
1. CSV File Upload
Provide a Browse button to upload a CSV file.
Display the uploaded file name.
Load the dataset into the application.
2. Dynamic Data Preprocessing

Implement a "Dynamic Preprocessing" button that automatically handles datasets with different structures and column names.

The preprocessing should automatically:

Detect numerical and categorical columns.
Handle missing values.
Encode categorical features.
Scale numerical features when required.
Remove duplicate rows.
Handle outliers (if applicable).
Separate input features (X) and target column (y).
Split data into training and testing datasets.
Perform all preprocessing without hardcoding any column names.

The application should work with any classification CSV dataset regardless of the number or names of its columns.

3. Download Preprocessed Dataset

Provide a "Download Preprocessed Data" button.

After preprocessing, users should be able to:

Download the cleaned and transformed dataset as a new CSV file.
Preserve all preprocessing changes (encoding, scaling, missing value handling, etc.).
Save the processed file with an appropriate filename (e.g., preprocessed_data.csv).
4. Classifier Selection

Provide a dropdown list containing at least 10 classification algorithms.

Include the following classifiers:

Logistic Regression
K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN)
Decision Tree
Random Forest
Support Vector Machine (SVM)
Naive Bayes
Gradient Boosting
AdaBoost
Extra Trees Classifier
XGBoost

Bonus Classifiers (Extra Credit):

LightGBM
CatBoost
HistGradientBoosting
Bagging Classifier
Voting Classifier
Stacking Classifier
Ridge Classifier
Passive Aggressive Classifier
SGD Classifier
Gaussian Process Classifier
5. Model Training

Provide a Train Model button that:

Trains the selected classifier.
Displays a progress/status message.
6. Model Evaluation

Display the following evaluation metrics:

Accuracy
Precision
Recall
F1-Score
Confusion Matrix
Classification Report
7. Prediction (Optional Bonus)

Allow users to:

Enter new sample values manually, or
Upload a separate CSV file for prediction.

Display the predicted class labels.

User Interface Requirements

The interface should contain:

Browse CSV Button
Selected File Name
Dynamic Preprocessing Button
Download Preprocessed Data Button
Classifier Dropdown
Train Model Button
Evaluate Model Button
Prediction Section (Bonus)
Results Panel
Confusion Matrix Display
Classification Report Display
Expected Workflow
Upload a CSV dataset.
Click Dynamic Preprocessing.
Review the processed data.
Click Download Preprocessed Data to save the cleaned dataset.
Select a classifier.
Train the model.
Evaluate the model.
View performance metrics.
(Bonus) Predict new data.
